"epic feature set" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-feature-set&gt;
		<header>What makes a details page a Feature Set: a ranked list to pick from, which you can put in your own order.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>A Feature Set is a page you answer on: a ranked list, a table for each section, three columns: Item, Your pick, Facts. <text code>&lt;epic-feature-set&gt;</> is the element that makes it one.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone writing a page you answer on, or changing this element.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph><label size="mini" color="green">built</> in <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-feature-set" link="/epic/src/components/epic-feature-set/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-feature-set/" code>epic-feature-set/</></> (epic <text code>epic-engine</> P80).</>

	<section label="1. Making a page">
		<icon slot="icon" name="terminal"/>
		<text paragraph>Never write one by hand: the command makes it from data.</>
		<markdown>
			```sh
			epic ask create my-list --template feature-set --epic my-epic --from my-list.json5
			```
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>The data: copy the starter, <text code>feature-set.json5</>, in the tool's templates.</>
			<item>The next round: <text code>epic ask round my-list --from my-list.json5</>. Each item keeps its name while it stays in its section.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="2. What it does">
		<icon slot="icon" name="hand pointer"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Names: sections are S1, S2 and each one's items F1, F2, so S1F1 names one item. A name stays with its item in its section, and is never used again. A round that moves an item to another section gives it a new one.</>
			<item>In the side bar and on a phone, Your pick comes first, then Item with its Facts under it.</>
			<item>Reorder sections, and Reorder on each section: one dialog, dragged by the dots or moved by the arrows. Cancel, the ✕ and Escape change nothing.</>
			<item>The order is part of the answer: Send tells Claude.</>
			<item>Each section takes the colour of its picks: red until every one is decided.</>
			<item>Links to other sites open a new tab; the rest open in the same window, and Back returns you to where you were.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Parts">
		<icon slot="icon" name="table columns"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Part</>
				<cell>What it is</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>base</>
				</>
				<cell>Its line: Reorder sections.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>reorder</>
				</>
				<cell>The Reorder sections button.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>dialog</>
				</>
				<cell>The dialog that reorders, a <text code>&lt;ui-modal&gt;</>.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>list</>
				</>
				<cell>The dialog's list.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>entry</>
				</>
				<cell>One row of that list: its handle, name, title and arrows.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>cancel</>
				</>
				<cell>The dialog's Cancel.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>save</>
				</>
				<cell>The dialog's Save order.</>
			</>
		</>
	</>
